# Honcho environment overrides (OPTIONAL).
#   cp .env.honcho.example .env.honcho
#
# You normally do NOT need this file. The compose files already configure Honcho
# to use the local Ollama service for everything:
#   - text features (deriver, dialectic, summary, dream) -> gemma4:e4b
#   - embeddings                                          -> mxbai-embed-large (1024-dim)
# and set a dummy LLM_OPENAI_API_KEY (Ollama ignores it).
#
# Pull both models once after first start:
#   docker compose exec ollama ollama pull gemma4:e4b
#   docker compose exec ollama ollama pull mxbai-embed-large
#
# Values set in the compose `environment:` take precedence over this file, so to
# override the model routing edit the `x-honcho-env` anchor in the compose file.
#
# NOTE on embedding dimensions: migrations create the pgvector column at 1536.
# The honcho entrypoint runs scripts/configure_embeddings.py to resize it to
# EMBEDDING_VECTOR_DIMENSIONS. The resize only works while embedding tables are
# empty, so set the dimension before ingesting data (or recreate the pg-data
# volume). If you change the embedding model, update both
# EMBEDDING_MODEL_CONFIG__MODEL and EMBEDDING_VECTOR_DIMENSIONS in the anchor.
#
# Use this file only for extra settings, e.g. enabling auth for production:
# AUTH_USE_AUTH=true
# AUTH_JWT_SECRET=...   # generate with: python scripts/generate_jwt_secret.py
